1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:05,112
2028 Los Angeles Olympics Gathers Momentum With Four Years to Go.

2
00:00:05,062 --> 00:00:17,887
With the Paris 2024 and Milan-Cortina 2026 Olympics in the rearview mirror, the Los Angeles 2028 Summer Games are rapidly taking shape as organizers finalize venues and infrastructure plans.

3
00:00:17,887 --> 00:00:31,075
LA28 officials confirmed that the opening ceremony will take place at SoFi Stadium in Inglewood, with athletics and track events returning to the historic Los Angeles Memorial Coliseum, which will host its third Olympic Games.

4
00:00:31,075 --> 00:00:39,850
The organizing committee announced a record $8.5 billion domestic sponsorship deal, surpassing all previous U.S.-hosted Games.

5
00:00:39,850 --> 00:00:46,987
Softball and flag football will debut as new sports, while surfing will return to the waters off Huntington Beach.

6
00:00:46,987 --> 00:00:58,375
The basketball tournament is expected to feature a U.S. men's team led by rising stars like Wembanyama, Jayson Tatum, and Anthony Edwards, facing a deeply talented international field.

7
00:00:58,375 --> 00:01:09,562
The 2026 World Cup co-hosted by the United States has already stress-tested LA's transportation and hospitality infrastructure, providing valuable lessons for Olympic organizers.

8
00:01:09,562 --> 00:01:18,150
LA28 Chair Casey Wasserman called the Games "an opportunity to showcase Los Angeles as the world's premier sports and entertainment capital.

